Hybrid Datasets for Breast Mass Classification

This repository is a derivative of mammo_dp:
https://github.com/RichardObi/mammo_dp
Upstream commit: 20caed79441855870bae6f7efca1cac0ca8bac7e

The upstream project accompanies:
Richard Osuala et al., "Enhancing the Utility of Privacy-Preserving Cancer
Classification using Synthetic Data," 2024.

The upstream software is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The original LICENSE file is retained in this repository.

Principal modifications for the present study include:

- deterministic, class-balanced sampling of synthetic mass patches;
- additive hybrid training with a fixed real training set;
- seed-specific configurations for eight full fine-tuning conditions;
- SLURM scripts for five-seed experiment arrays;
- evaluation on held-out CBIS-DDSM and external BCDR data; and
- per-seed, aggregate, and paired-difference result exports.

Medical imaging datasets and generated image files are not covered by the
software license and remain subject to their respective access and reuse terms.
